	)
	(text "BUTTON PRESS OUTPUT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 227.33 87.63 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6b5597e1-92be-5757-a951-d3f9a3b7a987")
	)
	(text_box "1. BTN = the Parking Safety button line (the \"pin 5 wire\" in the design chat). Its CON1 pin or PCB pad is NOT verified: the panel MCU may read the switch locally (docs/electronics.md). Trace the switch pads and measure idle/pressed voltage first. R3/R4/R5 assume BTN idles near VBAT (12-14.4 V) and is pulled to ~0 V when pressed; a stiff 5 V line would read ~1.06 V on GPIO3, right at the threshold."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 138.43 0)
		(size 78.74 21.59)
		(margins 1.27 1.27 1.27 1.27
		)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "90943cf2-a23b-5e47-a2be-5ca3ab10706a")
	)
	(text_box "2. TX is wired (GPIO6) so the board CAN transmit, but it is silent by default: R6 pulls SLNT high (TJA1051 transmitter off) during boot/reset, and firmware drives GPIO5 high and runs TWAI listen-only. It never sends unless the firmware is changed on purpose. Hard lock: cut the GPIO5 link, tie SLNT to 3V3.\n3. Set the CAN Pal 120R termination switch OFF: the car bus is already terminated.\n4. ESP32-C3 TWAI is classic CAN only; confirm the panel bus carries no CAN FD frames."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 96.52 138.43 0)
		(size 78.74 21.59)
		(margins 1.27 1.27 1.27 1.27
		)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "07c84f21-c230-55dc-b1b5-ea3d4c19f00e")
	)
	(text_box "6. GPIO2/8/9 are strapping pins (GPIO8 = onboard LED): leave unconnected. GPIO10 is not a strap; R2 holds Q1 off during boot. GPIO20/21 (UART0) kept free for serial debug.\n7. VBAT is tapped on the PCB side of the panel's reverse-polarity diodes D1/D2; one common ground with the panel (CON1-16). F1 limits fault current if D1 fails short. D2 blocks USB 5 V back-feeding U1. LM7805: 35 V max input; SMAJ18A clamps ~29 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 162.56 0)
		(size 160.02 11.43)
		(margins 1.27 1.27 1.27 1.27
		)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3b2c407a-92b8-5af9-b37c-3dde61404e9c")
	)
	(text_box "5. R3 = 200R gives 60-70 mA if BTN is a stiff 12-14 V node; raise to 470R-1k if the measured pull-up allows. Firmware ignores GPIO3 while Q1 is on and caps press time."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 138.43 0)
		(size 106.68 10.16)
		(margins 1.27 1.27 1.27 1.27
		)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "13674769-503d-5c42-a847-7e687d0522f5")
	)
